[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105408,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibrodysplasia ossificans progressiva (FOP) is a heritable condition of progressive soft tissue metamorphosis to bone, resulting in immobility and premature death.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105409,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<h5>MIM numbering</h5>\r\n<p>135100 Fibrodysplasia ossificans progressiva; FOP</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105410,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FB31.1 Fibrodysplasia ossificans progressiva</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105411,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> myositis ossificans progressiva.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105412,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105413,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FOP typically initially affects the dorsal axial and proximal regions, with later involvement of appendicular and caudal regions {31053156}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105414,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FOP is usually associated with congenital malformations of the great toes (bilateral hallux valgus, malformed first metatarsal bone) and cervical&ndash;vertebral fusions.</p>\r\n<p>Episodes of painful soft tissue swelling occur during the first decade of life, accompanied by relentless and progressive ossification of soft tissues. Traumas can accelerate the process, so the suspicion of FOP is a contraindication to biopsy. Progressive ossification of the chest wall causes respiratory insufficiency and death {31053156}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105415,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FOP affects 1&nbsp;in 2&nbsp;million people, with no racial or geographical preponderance {32988985}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105416,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FOP is associated with a germline activating mutation of the <em>ACVR1</em> gene {32730934}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105417,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases result from a de novo germline activating mutation of <em>ACVR1</em>, which encodes a BMP receptor {32730934; 16642017; 16831905; 32988985}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105418,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Soft tissue masses precede heterotopic ossification.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105419,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Early lesions of FOP are nonspecific vascular loose fibrous tissue proliferations with variable inflammation, which over time become more collagenized {11521229}. As the lesions mature, cartilage appears, followed by endochondral ossification. FOP cannot be distinguished histologically from localized myositis ossificans.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105420,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105421,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Molecular testing is necessary to demonstrate a germline mutation of <em>ACVR1</em> {32730934}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105422,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> congenital great toe malformations and rapidly progressive soft tissue masses preceding heterotopic ossification; demonstration of an <em>ACVR1</em> mutation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105423,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105424,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 520,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FOP is progressively disabling, leading to wheelchair use within the second decade of life. The median survival time is 56&nbsp;years {20194327}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:24:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]